PyHunt is a Python-only fork of VASH (Vanguard Agentic Security Harness), which
is itself derived from three prior works. Portions that carry an Apache-2.0
header in-file are licensed under Apache-2.0; all other code is under the MIT
License (see LICENSE). Full third-party license texts are in licenses/; the
per-component attribution is below.

What PyHunt changes relative to VASH: the analysis surface is restricted to
Python (the JavaScript/TypeScript, Java, Go and C# PoC runtimes and their
runtime observers are removed), and the decision that a proof-of-concept
proved something moves out of the Hunt agent's judgement and into deterministic
Python (pyhunt/scripts/oracle/), gated on a per-PoC nonce and on the observer's frame
attribution.

